---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import ArchitectureDiagram from "../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro";
---
<Marketing title="Architecture" description="How Goshikq splits a Rust execution runtime from Python and TypeScript SDKs, with independent goal verification." path="/architecture/">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Architecture</p>
    <h1>Runtime owns the loop. SDKs declare the work.</h1>
    <p class="lede">A model suggestion is never treated as a business result. After <code>POST /api/v1/runs</code> the SDK long-polls the worker protocol; Rust validates transitions, schemas, permissions, budgets, and verification.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <ArchitectureDiagram />
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Piece</th><th>Choice</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Runtime</td><td>Rust, Tokio, Axum, SQLx</td><td>Transitions, retries, persistence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Python SDK</td><td>goshikq_ai</td><td>Agents, tools, goals, StateProvider</td></tr>
          <tr><td>TypeScript SDK</td><td>@goshikq/sdk</td><td>Same worker protocol as Python</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Studio</td><td>Next.js</td><td>Observe persisted runs</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Store</td><td>PostgreSQL 16</td><td>Runs, events, evidence</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p><a href="/docs/core-concepts/">Architecture docs</a> · <a href="https://github.com/goshikavs/goshikq-agent-framework/blob/main/docs/decisions/ADR-001-runtime-boundaries.md">ADR-001</a></p>
  </section>
</Marketing>
